          "segment_id": "seg-7c66dc56f2d3f8a560caf956",
          "segment_index": 12,
          "source_segment_id": "seg-7c66dc56f2d3f8a560caf956",
          "source_text_sha256": "02ab292dc13b131b85392c4f9d3c0dbdad31bff67e7667b472fdf2c57b9e4156",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On August 5, 2013, at 11:14 PM, a couple observed the passage of a very bright point in the sky. This observation of a very bright point crossing the sky from West to East at the beginning of the night has all the characteristics of observing a large satellite: that evening, the passage of the International Space Station (ISS) was noted precisely at that time: from 11:11 PM to 11:16 PM (see the Calsky log). The fact that the witness states that the light \"at times seemed to deviate from its trajectory\" is likely the result of a visual perception illusion: seeing the movement of a bright point in the sky. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\": observation of the passage of the ISS.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "e47c14bee968175d44d4eabb66e9f0df9b93fa469b9f8a80478864fa7f243b20"
        }
